# Godot 4
.godot/
*.translation
export.cfg
*.tmp
build/

# The piposh-3d resource pack, built from `titles/piposh-3d` by
# `--export-pack Pack`. ~269 MB, and it is not new data: the same bytes already
# arrive with the submodule, so it is the import saved ahead of time rather
# than anything to store.
titles/*.pck
# The commit each pack was built from, so a submodule bump is detectable.
titles/*.pck.stamp
android/*.keystore
android/*.jks

# Broken keep-importer stubs — BMPs/WAVs load at runtime from source files
**/*.import

# Build artifacts / local logs
*.apk
smoke_log.txt

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local overrides
*.local
user://

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ScummVM reference sources, fetched by tools/fetch_scummvm_reference.sh.
# GPL-2.0-or-later, read for the model only — never vendored.
#
# No trailing slash, and that is the point rather than a typo. A pattern ending
# in `/` matches directories only, so `reference/scummvm/` left a *symlink* of
# that name untracked and visible -- which is how the tree gets into a worktree,
# since it is fetched rather than committed and a fresh worktree therefore never
# has it. `lingo_surface_audit` is the check that reads it, and it reports the
# absence as 0 builtins rather than as a missing directory. One `git add -A` away
# from committing a symlink into somebody's own checkout.
reference/scummvm
.traces/

# Screenshots the snapshot key writes. Somebody's session, of a game that is not
# ours to redistribute — the same reason `games/` is ignored below.
.snapshots/

# Save states, and the PNG written beside each one. Somebody's session again —
# and a save is a pile of member numbers only meaningful against the game it was
# taken in, so there is nothing here another checkout could use.
saves/

# Agent worktrees: full checkouts, 2.5 GB and counting. Never committed.
.claude/worktrees/

# Original Director game data lives in private Git submodules under `games/`.
# The public parent repository tracks only their gitlinks, not their contents.

# Titles being brought up against this engine, dropped in whole rather than
# added as submodules -- 795 MB at the time of writing. Not ours to redistribute,
# the same rule as `games/` above, and unlike `games/` there is no gitlink here
# to stop a `git add -A` from committing the contents outright.
test-games/

# Serialises concurrent `gate.sh` runs. Two at once swap each other's corpus
# mid-run and report another title's movies as this one's regressions.
.gate.lock/

# Agent scratch probes. Not ignored once, and a whole-file `git add` swept
# another agent's untracked work into an unrelated commit.
tools/scratch/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages.
# Per-plan working state, not a record -- git log is the record.
.superpowers/
